[00:31.15] In my rear view mirror
[00:34.09] The sun is going down
[00:36.96] 
[00:40.91] Sinking behind bridges in the road
[00:45.45] 
[00:51.19] I think of all the good things
[00:54.29] That we have left undone
[00:57.35] 
[00:59.95] And I suffer premonitions
[01:03.54] Confirm suspicions
[01:07.89] Of the holocaust to come
[01:11.99] 
[01:21.34] The rusty wire that holds the cork
[01:24.32] That keeps the anger in
[01:28.16] 
[01:30.99] Gives way and suddenly
[01:34.25] It's day again
[01:38.38] 
[01:41.12] The sun is in the east
[01:44.22] Even though the day is done
[01:50.45] Two suns in the sunset
[01:55.68] Could be the human race is run?
[02:05.57] 
[02:19.75] Like the moment when the brakes lock
[02:23.08] And you slide towards the big truck (oh no)
[02:26.15] You stretch the frozen moments with your fear
[02:30.97] 
[02:33.25] And you'll never hear their voices (daddy, daddy!)
[02:37.19] And you'll never see their faces
[02:40.40] You have no recourse to the law anymore
[02:46.09] 
[03:02.66] As the windshield melts and my tears evaporate
[03:12.34] Leaving only charcoal to defend
[03:18.88] 
[03:22.51] Finally I understand the feelings of the few
[03:31.33] Ashes and diamonds
[03:35.66] Foe and friend
[03:38.95] We were all equal in the end
[03:41.39] 